 ],
 "text": "Hand washing was chipping Josephine Cochran's heirloom china. Her 1886 patent cleaned dishes with water pressure, instead of scrubbing. Wire racks held plates, glasses and knives in place inside a crate. A hand lever pumped soapy jets while the crate slowly turned. Then hot water rinsed and the dishes dried from their own heat. Lesson, notice everyday friction. It can inspire an invention. Download RM to support livelihood tools."
